  "interpretation": [
    "The same 82 victim requests remain. Runway reduces repeated episodes from 38 to 4 and observed next-schedule re-preemption from 24 to 0; FIFO retained 25 next-schedule repeats.",
    "The 63 deferred policy decisions never call native allocation and are not native allocation None. Of these, 55 fit the candidate-plus-one term alone but fail the combined resident-plus-candidate headroom condition.",
    "Zero immediate re-preemption among 86 actual resumes supports the intended one-step behavior on this trajectory. It does not show that each deferred decision would otherwise immediately re-preempt, and four later repeat episodes remain.",
    "About 94.7% of the reduction in emitted scheduled tokens is fewer repeated positions; the remaining net change is generated output length. This is work accounting, not a GPU-time causal decomposition.",
    "Parent pair analysis finds lower mean completion time and improvement on the 802 identical-output requests, so the observation is broader than makespan alone. Other requests changing length can still affect this subset through shared execution.",
    "The native 0236 tail still changes from length-truncated 1024 tokens to naturally stopped 293 tokens; the entire 4.90-second makespan decrease cannot be credited to the gate.",
    "This remains a single evolved-trajectory comparison with a one-step gate, not a persistent reservation or protected-run guarantee."
  ]
